From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 14:19:29 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(glm cuda): a stopped request ends on every rank within a
 round

The GLM decode loops (serial, MTP, DFlash2, auto) call on_tokens but never read its result, and rank 1 runs
with a no-op callback, so rank 1 cannot know that rank 0 wants to stop. After a client left, a stop string
matched or a grammar cut, both ranks decoded on to max_tokens or an end token, and every later request
waited behind it.

stop.StopVote wraps on_tokens. Rank 0's wish to stop rides as one extra float32 word on the next verify
sample's all-gather (the exchange each round already makes; the nucleus rule's first gather likewise) and
is removed before sampling, so every rank ends the run after the same round. Sampled tokens are unchanged;
only when a stopped run ends changes. Every rank adds the word to the same gathers, so gather sizes stay
equal across ranks. GlmEngine._run_once sets the vote on every rank after prefill, _run clears it, and the
stats of a stopped run say "stopped". One rank stops the same way.

Tests: tests/test_glm_serial_stop.py (two CPU ranks as threads over a real all-gather: every loop and
sampling rule, replies unchanged, equal gather sizes; GlmEngine._run on two ranks) and a GPU case in
tests/cuda/test_glm_engine.py.

